<title>RUSSIA: Russian 287-day T-bill yields 30.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 287-day T-bill yields 30.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 287-day discount Treasury bills was 30.01 percent at an auction on Wedensday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield between 30.59 and 36.02 percent.</p>
<p>The series 22070 bills, maturing on November 19, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed at 31.06 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Both the 22070 bills and the new issue are subject to a new 15-percent tax on government securities.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number			     22072</p>
<p>    Issue volume				7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			     1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			   11.04 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)			    6.91 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				    5.59 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			     80.91 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		   80.91 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			     30.01 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		  30.01 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor					 287 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			     Nov 26, 1997</p>
<p>On February 12, the finance ministry will also offer 4.50 trillion roubles in 196-day T-bills (series 22071).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 7.66 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22042).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
